+# Change
+
+`gen.py` `hr_target()` now emits `{"units": "%lthr", "start": lo, "end": hi}`
+instead of `{"units": "%lthr", "value": lo, "end": hi}`.
+
+# Why (hypothesis, NOT verified)
+
+The old body used `value` + `end`. In Intervals.icu's workout_doc a range target
+is `start`/`end`; `value` is the single-point form. With `value` set, the range
+appears not to be treated as a custom corridor, and the Garmin export falls back
+to the watch's zone bands, which matches readback/watch-notes.md (every step shows
+a zone edge pair, and changing the watch's LTHR only moved the bands). The API
+accepting the event (steps populated) doesn't show the range was understood.
+
+# Not verified
+
+I couldn't confirm the field names from Intervals docs (the forum page I fetched
+only covers the text syntax) and didn't push anything (no external calls). Please
+regenerate, push, and re-read the event and the watch. Expected: Tempo 151–160,
+Float 129–141, etc. If the watch still shows zones, the next thing to try is the
+documented text syntax (e.g. `- 8m 88-93% LTHR`) in the event `description`,
+which Intervals parses itself.
